WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
Hi, I'm Bruce Daisley. I work at Twitter but
in my spare time

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:11.190
I've been studying work culture and how
we can be happier at work.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:15.719
Work has become this sort of colossal game of Jenga where we're trying to add things

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:20.880
on top or still keep everything standing
up and stable. I've put together some

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:27.359
thoughts on ways that we can make our
lives a lot less stressful.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.960
Half of all people who have checked their emails outside of work hours show signs of high

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.430
levels of stress. The very easiest thing
you can do to reduce your stress levels

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.739
from work is take the number off your
email app that single act is the

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.000
simplest thing we can do to reduce our
stress levels.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:50.160
The second best change that anyone can make is to take a lunch break. The habit of eating 'al desco' has

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.420
become so common now it's contributing
to an increase in our stress levels and

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.780
I understand when you're sitting at your
desk you're thinking you've got a

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.530
hundred emails left walking away and
taking a break can feel really

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:05.580
counter-intuitive but scientists have
found the best way to ensure that you

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.650
feel energised is to take that pause.  You
might want to try a monk mode morning.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.890
More and more of us are finally get hard
to get things done because of all the

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.610
interruptions. A guy called Cal Newport
who's a professor at Georgetown

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.590
University in Washington, he wrote a book
called Deep Work and one of the ideas he

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.479
gave was that we should think about
having a monk mode morning.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.619
Well monk mode is where we go somewhere that is silent, there's no interruptions, we maybe

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:36.180
get a block of ninety minutes work done,
maybe twice a week, then we go to the

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.049
office as normal, added advantages we've
missed the commute, and got our emails

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:41.746
and our meetings done.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Some interesting research from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.950
shows that one
of the best ways to increase workplace

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.390
creativity is to increase the amount of
chat, and actually that can be chat about

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:58.560
last night's TV that can be chat about
what's happening in sports games because

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.490
normally those conversations then lead
to work discussions. It's a strange thing

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.210
that by encouraging people to have more
chats we're actually going to be

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.410
achieving more at work. But the research
seems to suggest that the most creative

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:15.190
offices are the ones that chat
the most. Ben Waber, one of the researchers,

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.420
said that one of the best ways to
increase creativity in your office is to

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.870
move the location of the coffee machine. By having the coffee machine, the kettle,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.770
the water cooler, in a different place
you'll actually lead to more people

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.298
having discussions, conversations.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.500
Scientists have found that one of the biggest barriers to being creative in our jobs is stress,

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.420
and all of us with our phones feel more stressed than ever before.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.040
You need to give yourself permission to have a digital Sabbath, to take time away from your work

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.080
at the weekend,
for a bit of refreshment, a bit of

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.980
renewal. Discourage your boss from
emailing at the weekend because it leads

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.500
to people feeling anxious when they come
back to work on Monday.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.900
Anxious people can't be creative.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.090
I think in the current
world we often celebrate overwork and

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:05.560
people working long hours. The magazine
profiles we read, the TV profiles we see are

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.090
about people who work these enormous
long working weeks. And in fact all of

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.900
the evidence is starting to point to the
fact that maybe that's not the best idea.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.730
Maybe 40 hours of work a week is the
right amount. Use our breaks and our

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.630
evenings as times to re-energise
ourselves so when we come back to our

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.000
desks we're full of life. Doing 40 hours
of work is probably enough.

